        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 7238,
      "author": {
        "id": 1324603
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T08:53:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is 6.1 kernel, I suppose we could sync the change as android15-6.1. However, for older kernel (5.15/5.10), the tricky part is the default value of \"allowed\". To make it work in 7228 if trace_android_rvh_set_user_nice is not registered, it has to be default false, but if we change it to \"if (!allowed)\" here, it will bail out if trace_android_rvh_set_user_nice_locked is not registered. In our current vendor hook, we just change the task prio but updates the task nice without touching allowed, so \"task_nice(p) \u003d\u003d nice\" will be true and the code will bailed out, that\u0027s why I kept the whole thing originally, but we don\u0027t need to check \"nice \u003c MIN_NICE || nice \u003e MAX_NICE\" again for sure. I think setting the default value of allowed to true and modify 7228 to \"if ((task_nice(p) \u003d\u003d nice || nice \u003c MIN_NICE || nice \u003e MAX_NICE) \u0026\u0026 allowed)\" is better, but I\u0027m not sure if it will break other vendor\u0027s code, or we could change it to \"if (allowed)\" here, including android15-6.1 and keep allowed default false.",
      "parentUuid": "e39517e6_a696e858",
      "revId": "27afa66b1b8e439c5ecc4badeeffd7ee69378977",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42b976d3_1ab5324d",
